<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Diaspora.Modules.Creator</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Diaspora.Modules.Creator</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The Creator Platform (Phase B18.x). The eleven creator-economy capabilities the frontend's
      Phase 7 register found no contract behind, implemented as one module rather than eleven:
      the creator projection and its status ladder, the creator-programme verification wrapper,
      milestones, challenges, community grants, the Academy, the referral programme, the sign-up
      point bonus, the reward rules and redemption catalogue, the leaderboards and the creator
      directory.

      The register's own finding is this module's premise: "Phase 7 is not sixteen unrelated holes,
      it is one missing backend module ... and the eleven share a single aggregate — a creator
      projection with a status, a programme membership and a progress store."

      What the Creator Platform owns: the creator profile and its server-decided status, the
      creator-programme application and its eleven-state machine, milestone definitions and per
      creator progress, challenge definitions and enrolments, grant programmes with server-defined
      application forms and the applications against them, Academy content as structured blocks
      with server-side quiz grading and versioned progress, referral codes and the qualification
      rule behind them, the sign-up bonus, the reward rules catalogue and redemption records, and
      the recognised-activity ledger every one of those reads.

      What it deliberately does not own, and never duplicates:

        Identity is Trust's. This module asks ITrustService whether a member's identity is verified
        and whether their account stands in good order; it stores no document, no evidence content
        and no KYC state, and creator verification is a separate state machine from Trust's.

        Money is B15's. Points are B15's too — RewardAccount is the platform's single points
        ledger, and this module awards points by publishing RewardPointsGrantedIntegrationEvent
        and spends them through B15's own IRewardPointsAccount seam. There is no second balance,
        no second ledger and no wallet write anywhere in this assembly.

        Delivery is B13's. This module publishes integration events and composes no notification.

        Ranking for recommendation is B14's. The creator leaderboard is a ranking of this module's
        own recognised-activity ledger against a served score definition, which is a different
        thing from a recommendation surface.

        Analytics is B19's. There is no view, impression, reach or engagement figure in this
        module and no time-series API. The recognised-activity ledger records actions the creator
        programme rewards, not audience behaviour.

      Idempotency is B15's primitive, copied rather than reinvented: a nullable key column on the
      aggregate the write creates, uniquely indexed, looked up before the write and replayed on a
      repeat. There is no second idempotency store.

      Registers entirely through B2.6 contributor interfaces: no edit to the Platform Kernel, to
      Identity, or to Program.cs.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    One module reference, and it is narrow.

    Financial, for reward points. B15's RewardAccount is the platform's single points balance and
    its own documentation names "a creator platform" as the grantor the seam exists for. This
    module awards by publishing a contract B15 already consumes, and debits a redemption through
    B15's IRewardPointsAccount — the seam added for this phase — so the balance check and the
    debit are one transaction rather than two hopeful ones. It creates no payment, no wallet, no
    ledger entry and no conversion, and an architecture test asserts it.

    Notably absent: Trust, Community, Guides, Community Life, Notifications and Recommendations.
    Trust is reached through the kernel's ITrustService, which is what that abstraction is for.
    Everything a milestone, a challenge or a leaderboard counts arrives as a published integration
    event, which is why this module can rank a creator's contribution without referencing the
    module that produced it.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.SharedKernel\Diaspora.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Contracts\Diaspora.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Platform\Diaspora.Platform.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Application\Diaspora.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Persistence\Diaspora.Persistence.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Financial\Diaspora.Modules.Financial.csproj" />

    <!--
      B23.x Wave 12. Community owns the follow graph — `FollowTargetType.Member` is how somebody
      follows a creator — and this module's automation scope authority has to page through a creator's
      audience to broadcast to it. Community composes at 500 and this module at 1400, so the edge runs
      in the permitted direction, and it is the same shape B12 already has for `ICommunityContentSource`.

      Nothing else in this module reads it: the reference exists for the follower page and the
      follower count behind `notify.followers`, and an architecture test would report any other use.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Community\Diaspora.Modules.Community.csproj" />

    <!--
      20 Oct 2026. A creator's cover is one of the member's own image uploads, and only Media can
      confirm it is theirs and make it public (`PublishProfileImageCommand`, sent in-process as
      Providers sends `AttachMediaCommand`). Media composes at 400, so the edge runs in the
      permitted direction. Used by the cover handlers and nothing else.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Media\Diaspora.Modules.Media.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
